==='''Insane Trials'''===
These trials work a bit differently than prior trials, as they must be completed in order. To unlock a trial, you must get the respective level to unlock it on weapons in Polish Prestige (under Unity → Minerals, must get a level 30 mineral to unlock).
{| class="wikitable" style="text-align:center; font-size: 1rem"
!Trial
!Unlock
!Goal
!Handicap
!Reward
|-
|Insane Trial 1
| Level 25 Knuckles
| Buy 65 DTP
| First DU is useless and dilation penalties are ^2 stronger.
| You get 10 more EC from trials
|-
|Insane Trial 2
| Level 50 Spear
| Unite with e5.8M+ score
| Common Exponent is divided by 1M
| Now you keep all of your EC on Unity Reset. Trials reward is changed to PP gain mult.
|-
|Insane Trial 3
| Level 50 Knuckles
| Reach Unity
| IP and EP gains are much worse now. DP Gain is multiplied by Min(1, Eternities amount). Reset eternites amount to 0 on Unity Reset.
| Get additional 100% of IP and EP per second passively
|-
|Insane Trial 4
| Level 100 Axe
| Reach 2.018e705+ EP and 8.14e2025+ IP
| All EC rewards are much worse now and actually are penalties.
| You can complete 1 more difficulty for each EC. EC past 50 boost your magnet gain chance
|-
|Insane Trial 5
| Level 100 Bow
| Reach 65 DTP
| DU1 is disabled. Dilation Penalties and DP gain scales much harsher.
| Dilation's best score is automatically set to your current score raised to DU Power Penalty
|-
|Insane Trial 6
| Level 100 Knuckles
| Reach Attack Level 100
| Attack Divider and Level Scalings are harsher, R13 is inverted, Gold and Ascend Strength is logarithmed. Attack Stats are wiped on Unity.
| Passively gain 1 Unity per second, multiplied by Minerals' Game Speed
|} 

